<title>USA: Morton buys majority of French salt firm.</title>
<headline>Morton buys majority of French salt firm.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morton International Inc said on Thursday it purchased two-thirds of the stock of Compagnie des Salins du Midi et des Salines de l'Est for $180 million.</p>
<p>The purchase is in keeping with terms of a definitive agreement signed in December between Morton and the principal shareholders of the French company:  Cie de Suez unit Suez Industrie, the Credit Agricole Group and the Rougie family.</p>
<p>Salins du Midi is a salt producer whose combined sales are about $870 million.</p>
<p>Morton manufactures and markets specialty chemicals, automotive inflatable restraint systems and salt.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
